  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "JpU+aNvxQ3pCtFV11uKu5HH/RMQ=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:40.148Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The release notes for 2025.2.01, dated 16 December 2025, state: *\"Added support to see the business audit trail of a case or process instance.\"* The Enterprise `AuditService` documentation asserts *\"Created AuditInstances are immutable\"*, with a builder carrying `creatorId()` for user attribution, `type()`, `subType()` and `payload()`, stored in `flw_audit_instance` and publishable as an audit stream.\n\nControlled code search confirms which side of the line it falls on: `AuditService`, `AuditInstance` and `flw_audit_instance` each return zero hits in `flowable-engine`, against 628 for `HistoryService` as a control. The capability is Enterprise-only, and it exists.\n\nAny pitch asserting that Flowable has no immutable business audit log is factually wrong against the commercial product. The claim survives only when scoped explicitly to the Apache-2.0 edition.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T08:45:40.148745Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T08:45:40.148754Z"
    }
  },
